producer_report.summary:
I added a guard so Athena's pushes, replaces and branch deletes reach only the repository's own `origin`, and recorded it as OLY-B-BND-01's mechanism. fmt, clippy and the tests I ran pass. I did not re-run `xtask --test policy` or the whole workspace after the last test-only edit.

`Git::own_origin_url` in athena-git refuses any remote name but `origin`. It also refuses a missing origin, more than one fetch URL or push URL, and fetch and push URLs that name different repositories. It never echoes a URL. `push_branch` and `push_if_remote_at` call it first, so the records writer's pushes are covered too. `guard_origin_write` in gh/remote.rs wraps it and runs first in `GitRemote` push, replace and delete_branch.

Pull request calls read origin through the same guard. `own_origin_repository` accepts only an https github.com origin. `Athena::land_pr` and the early step use it. `push_ci_branch` prints a separate skip line when origin exists but is refused.

Behavior change: `athena land --pr` now refuses ssh and scp-style GitHub origins that `parse_remote` used to accept. The CHANGELOG line says so.

New tests cover:
- writes to a second remote, with a raw-push control and unchanged refs;
- no origin;
- two push URLs;
- two fetch URLs;
- a push URL on another repository;
- the `own_origin_repository` cases;
- the early-step cases with a single-URL control;
- the `land_pr` read order, as a source-text check of order only;
- the spec entry;
- the athena-git twins, including a hook test that shows git's own failure stays a `GitError::Failed`.

With the guard call removed from `GitRemote::push`, 6 of the 8 `git_remote` tests failed. I restored it.

The first workspace run showed one failure: my hook test used `set_permissions`, which `athena-testkit`'s `no_in_process_exec_writes` forbids. I switched it to `athena_testkit::write_executable`, and that test and `cargo test -p athena-git` now pass. `docs/spec.toml` changes only the mechanism and measure of OLY-B-BND-01, and CHANGELOG.md has one new Unreleased line.
